---
import "../styles/global.css";
// After global.css on purpose: a text style must win a tie with a global
// component rule on the same element (see the ORDER note in type.css).
import "../styles/type.css";
---

<nav transition:persist="navbar">
  {
    /* THREE PILLS ON A DESKTOP (2026-10-14, Josh: "on desktop it should be 3
      pills that are directly selectable"). The links stand in a row on the
      header's line at the right, always shown; the button is not drawn. (From
      2026-10-12 they were behind a MENU button there.)
      A HAMBURGER ON A PHONE (2026-10-13, Josh: "actually a hamburger will be
      better"): the same button, drawn as three black bars on the bare page
      that turn into a cross while it is open; the word MENU stays in the
      markup, clipped, as the button's name. The three black chips Josh asked
      for are what it opens. The links keep their ids, the script below still
      sets their labels, their targets and which of LOGIN / PROFILE shows. */
  }
  <button
    type="button"
    class="nav-menu-btn"
    id="nav-menu-btn"
    aria-expanded="false"
    aria-controls="nav-menu"
  >
    <span class="nav-menu-btn__label">MENU</span>
    <span class="nav-burger" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
    <img class="nav-menu-btn__pic" alt="" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" />
  </button>
  {
    /* BACK TO THE PORTFOLIOS FROM THE ACCOUNT PAGES (2026-10-31, Josh: "the
      vscn should lead back to the about page ... also add a back to
      portfolios button when you are on any of the acount pages"). VSCN
      opens Info, so the profile editor and the sign-in pages, which have no
      directory bar, get this key: centred in the header row, shown only on
      nav[data-account] (set by the script below). It was on every page
      from 2026-10-28 to 10-29. Info has the views switcher instead
      (ViewsPill.astro). */
  }
  <a href="/community" class="nav-portfolios" id="nav-portfolios"
    ><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path></svg><span>PORTFOLIOS</span></a
  >
  <div class="nav-links" id="nav-menu">
    <a href="/info" class="nav-link" id="nav-info">INFO</a>
    <a href="/community" class="nav-link nav-center" id="nav-community">COMMUNITY</a>
    {
      /* THE MENU IS A HIERARCHY ON A PHONE (2026-10-25, Josh: "the menu
        should hierarchially stack the community info and profile tabs"):
        each destination in the sheet's large type, its own pages under it a
        size down — Community's three views here, Profile's three tabs in
        .nav-acct below. Not drawn on a desktop, where the bar picks the view. */
    }
    <div class="nav-sub" id="nav-views">
      <a href="/community" class="nav-link nav-link--sub nav-link--view" data-pattern="">PORTFOLIOS</a>
      <a href="/community?pattern=grid" class="nav-link nav-link--sub nav-link--view" data-pattern="grid">IMAGES</a>
      <a href="/community?pattern=index" class="nav-link nav-link--sub nav-link--view" data-pattern="index">PEOPLE</a>
    </div>
    <div class="nav-right-group">
      <a href="/login" class="nav-link" id="nav-join">LOGIN</a>
      {
        /* THE MEMBER'S OWN FACE (2026-10-25, Josh: "the profile button
          smaller on desktop and when logged in your profile pic"): once
          signed in, the pill is the avatar Auth holds (profile.ts copies the
          saved photo there), a round picture on the header's line; with no
          photo yet it stays the word, in a smaller chip than SIGN UP. The
          phone's sheet keeps the word either way. */
      }
      <a
        href="/profile"
        class="nav-link nav-link--pill nav-link--profile"
        id="nav-profile"
        style="display:none;"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="nav-acct"
      >
        <span class="nav-profile__word">PROFILE</span>
        <img class="nav-profile__pic" alt="" width="30" height="30" decoding="async" />
      </a>
      {
        /* THE ACCOUNT MENU (2026-10-25, Josh: "the 3 tabs should be in the
          menu when clicking on the … icon", "EN DE should be in the menu
          that open upon clicking the profile button"). Signed in, the
          profile button opens this on a desktop: the editor's three tabs and
          the language switch. On a phone the tabs are lines of the sheet
          instead of PROFILE. On the editor page a tab line switches the tab
          in place; anywhere else it opens /profile on that tab (?tab=). */
      }
      <div class="nav-acct" id="nav-acct" style="display:none;">
        <a href="/profile?tab=profile" class="nav-link nav-link--tab nav-link--sub" id="nav-tab-profile" data-tab="profile"
          >PROFILE</a
        >
        <a href="/profile?tab=work" class="nav-link nav-link--tab nav-link--sub" id="nav-tab-work" data-tab="work">WORK</a>
        <a href="/profile?tab=account" class="nav-link nav-link--tab nav-link--sub" id="nav-tab-account" data-tab="account"
          >ACCOUNT</a
        >
        <a href="/de" class="nav-link nav-link--lang nav-acct__lang" id="nav-acct-lang">
          <span class="lang-cur">EN</span><span class="lang-sep"> / </span><span class="lang-tgt">DE</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <a href="/onboarding" class="nav-link nav-link--pill" id="nav-signup">SIGN UP</a>
    </div>
    {
      /* The language switch's place on the phone's sheet (2026-10-20): the
        fixed .lang-toggle below is hidden on every page with a footer, so the
        sheet carries its own copy, kept in step by updateNavLinks. On a
        desktop the corner one is the only switch again (2026-10-26, Josh:
        "smaller and in the bottom right corner on desktop"). */
    }
    <a href="/de" class="nav-link nav-link--lang" id="nav-sheet-lang">
      <span class="lang-cur">EN</span><span class="lang-sep"> / </span><span class="lang-tgt"
        >DE</span
      >
    </a>
  </div>
</nav>

<a href="/de" class="lang-toggle" id="nav-lang" transition:persist="lang-toggle">
  <span class="lang-cur">EN</span><span class="lang-sep"> / </span><span class="lang-tgt">DE</span>
</a>

{
  /* Persisted navigation keeps its DOM across page swaps, including its old
     scope attributes after a deployment. Stable selectors keep the new page's
     stylesheet matching those links. */
}
<style is:global>
  /* ON THE HEADER'S LINE, AT THE RIGHT (2026-10-12, Josh: "the header should
     be inline with the Menu buttons"). The title is one VSCN at the left of a
     --header-h tall row (Layout.astro); the nav is fixed over that row's
     right end, so the two read as one header and neither moves on scroll.
     Nothing is painted behind it: the row has no fill and no veil
     (2026-10-13, Josh), the page scrolls under the bare title and the black
     chips. Type for the button and the links is the NAV voice in type.css;
     this file sets boxes and colours only.
     THE KNOBS: --nav-ink / --nav-paper are the chips' two colours (black on
     white type, the current page inverted), --nav-chip-pad the chip's box. */
  nav[data-astro-transition-persist="navbar"] {
    --nav-ink: var(--color-dark);
    --nav-paper: var(--color-bg);
    --nav-chip-pad: 8px 10px 7px;
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: 30;
    height: var(--header-h);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding-right: 15px;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  /* MENU, the desktop trigger: black, white type (2026-10-13, Josh: "desktop
     menu: black background with white type"); underlined under the pointer
     and while open, like the links. */
  .nav-menu-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--nav-chip-pad);
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--nav-ink);
    color: var(--nav-paper);
    font-family: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .nav-menu-btn:hover,
  .nav-menu-btn[aria-expanded="true"] {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .nav-menu-btn:focus-visible {
    outline: 1.5px solid var(--nav-ink);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* THE HAMBURGER: three bars in a 16 x 12 box, drawn on a phone only. Open,
     the outer two slide to the middle and turn through 45 degrees into a
     cross while the middle one shrinks away. The turn overshoots on the
     site's one springy curve (the same the current page's chip wipes in on),
     and the middle bar leaves first so the cross is never drawn over a third
     line. */
  .nav-burger {
    display: none;
    position: relative;
    width: 16px;
    height: 12px;
  }
  .nav-burger i {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 2px;
    background: currentColor;
    transition:
      transform 0.42s cubic-bezier(0.2, 1.25, 0.35, 1) 0.04s,
      opacity 0.12s ease 0.04s;
  }
  .nav-burger i:nth-child(1) {
    top: 0;
  }
  .nav-burger i:nth-child(2) {
    top: 5px;
    transition-delay: 0.1s;
  }
  .nav-burger i:nth-child(3) {
    top: 10px;
  }
  .nav-menu-btn[aria-expanded="true"] .nav-burger i:nth-child(1) {
    transform: translateY(5px) rotate(45deg);
  }
  .nav-menu-btn[aria-expanded="true"] .nav-burger i:nth-child(2) {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: scaleX(0);
    transition-delay: 0s;
  }
  .nav-menu-btn[aria-expanded="true"] .nav-burger i:nth-child(3) {
    transform: translateY(-5px) rotate(-45deg);
  }

  /* The drop-down: the three chips stacked under the button, its right edge
     on the button's.
     IT ANIMATES BOTH WAYS (2026-10-13, Josh: "pay attention to the
     animation"). It used to be toggled with `hidden`, so it could only
     appear with a one-shot keyframe and it vanished with no motion at all.
     Now the button's aria-expanded is the single state: the list is
     `visibility: hidden` while closed (out of the tab order and the
     accessibility tree, and not clickable), and each chip is a transition on
     opacity and transform. They arrive top to bottom, 55ms apart, dropping
     in with the spring curve; they leave bottom to top, 30ms apart, faster
     and without the spring. Visibility changes at the END of the close, once
     the last chip has gone: the 0.3s below has to stay above the longest
     leave (last chip's delay 60ms + 0.2s). */
  .nav-links {
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(100% - 6px);
    right: 15px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    width: 10rem;
    visibility: hidden;
    transition: visibility 0s linear 0.3s;
  }
  .nav-menu-btn[aria-expanded="true"] ~ .nav-links {
    visibility: visible;
    transition-delay: 0s;
  }
  #nav-info {
    --i: 0;
  }
  #nav-community {
    --i: 1;
  }
  #nav-views,
  #nav-join,
  #nav-profile {
    --i: 2;
  }
  #nav-signup,
  #nav-acct {
    --i: 3;
  }

  /* Each link is a black chip with white type, square (the site has no
     radii), with a hairline the same black so the inverted chip below keeps
     an edge. */
  .nav-link {
    position: relative;
    /* The link's own stacking context, so the active chip's wipe (::before,
       z-index -1) paints over the chip's fill and under the type. */
    isolation: isolate;
    display: block;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: var(--nav-chip-pad);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--nav-paper);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--nav-ink);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--nav-ink);
    /* Closed: lifted and clear. Leaves last-first (see the drop-down above). */
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-8px);
    transition:
      color 0.25s ease 0.08s,
      opacity 0.14s ease calc((2 - var(--i, 0)) * 30ms),
      transform 0.2s ease calc((2 - var(--i, 0)) * 30ms);
  }
  .nav-menu-btn[aria-expanded="true"] ~ .nav-links .nav-link {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
    transition:
      color 0.25s ease 0.08s,
      opacity 0.2s ease calc(30ms + var(--i, 0) * 55ms),
      transform 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.2, 1.25, 0.35, 1) calc(30ms + var(--i, 0) * 55ms);
  }

  /* WHITE ON BLACK EVEN ONCE VISITED (2026-10-14, Josh: "the text is black on
     black bg"). global.css resets links with `a, a:visited { color: inherit }`,
     and a:visited (0,1,1) outranks .nav-link (0,1,0): every page the reader
     had already been to inherited the nav's black and vanished into the chip.
     A fresh browser has no history, and getComputedStyle reports :visited
     links as unvisited on purpose, so neither a clean test run nor a script
     can see this; look at it after visiting the pages. The current page's
     own :visited rule below comes later and still wins. */
  .nav-link:visited {
    color: var(--nav-paper);
  }

  /* THE CURRENT PAGE IS THE INVERTED CHIP: a paper capsule with a black
     hairline and black type. It wipes in (2026-10-12, "make the animation
     more flashy!"): a layer under the type that sweeps across the chip from
     the left.
     A CAPSULE LIKE THE CHIP (2026-10-14, Josh: "take a close look at the UI
     again"). Since the chips went round (global.css, CONTROLS) this layer
     stayed a square: it covered the capsule's hairline, so the current page
     read as loose black text on desktop and as a box with broken sides on a
     phone. It now takes the chip's radius (global.css excludes it from the
     square reset) and carries the hairline itself, and the wipe is a
     clip-path instead of a scaleX, which would squash the round ends. */
  .nav-link::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--nav-paper);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--nav-ink);
    clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0);
    transition: clip-path 0.28s cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.75, 0);
  }

  /* No grey and no thicker line under the pointer: the type underlines. */
  .nav-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }

  .nav-link--active,
  .nav-link--active:visited,
  .nav-link--active:hover {
    color: var(--nav-ink);
  }
  .nav-link--active::before {
    clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0);
    transition: clip-path 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.9, 0.2, 1) 0.05s;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .nav-link::before,
    .nav-link--active::before,
    .nav-burger i,
    .nav-links,
    .nav-link,
    .nav-menu-btn[aria-expanded="true"] ~ .nav-links .nav-link {
      transition: none !important;
    }
  }

  .nav-link:focus-visible {
    outline: 1.5px solid var(--color-dark);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* LOGIN and PROFILE share the third bar — only one of them is shown. */
  .nav-right-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  /* THREE PILLS, NO MENU, ON A DESKTOP (2026-10-14, Josh: "on desktop it
     should be 3 pills that are directly selectable"). The drop-down above is
     the phone's; here the same list is a row in the header's flow, always
     shown, and the button is not drawn. The open/closed machinery is
     switched off rather than removed: the list is visible, each pill is at
     rest, and only the type's colour and the current page's wipe animate.
     Two classes on the pill outrank the closed state (.nav-link, one class)
     whatever the button says, so a phone's open menu carried across the
     breakpoint changes nothing here. */
  @media (--bp-desktop) {
    /* IN FROM THE CORNER (2026-10-23, Josh: "weird to find them all the way
       in the corner"): the row ends where main's text does, --shell-max
       centred plus main's 15px gutter, not on the window's edge; the title
       starts on the mirror edge (Layout.astro). A window narrower than the
       measure keeps the old 15px. */
    /* LIKE COSMOS (2026-10-23, Josh: "do it like cosmos. left the
       different things we can select in the middle vscn ... on the right
       login as a pill", then "also with sign up and login"): the nav spans
       the row, the destinations at its left, the account at its right —
       LOGIN as a word and SIGN UP as a black pill, or PROFILE as the pill
       once signed in — and the title centred between them (Layout.astro).
       The row lets clicks through to the title; only the links take them. */
    nav[data-astro-transition-persist="navbar"] {
      left: 0;
      /* TO THE WINDOW'S EDGES (2026-10-26, Josh's top-bar mock): the title at
         the left and the account at the right, both on --header-side, no
         longer on main's text edges. */
      padding: 0 var(--header-side);
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link {
      pointer-events: auto;
    }
    .nav-menu-btn {
      display: none;
    }
    /* NO INFO / COMMUNITY IN A DESKTOP'S HEADER (2026-10-27, Josh, on the
       top-bar mock: "drop INFO/COMMUNITY from the desktop header"): VSCN
       goes home and the account stands alone at the right. The phone's sheet
       keeps both words. */
    #nav-info,
    #nav-community {
      display: none;
    }
    .nav-links {
      position: static;
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      width: auto;
      visibility: visible;
      transition: none;
    }
    .nav-links {
      flex: 1;
    }
    .nav-right-group {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-left: auto;
    }
    /* PLAIN TEXT, NOT PILLS (2026-10-20, Josh: "desktop stays for now,
       just replace with normal text"): the black capsules are gone, the
       three words stand on the paper, and the current page is underlined
       where the chip used to invert. The wipe layer is not drawn.
       NARROWER (2026-10-23, Josh: "navbar on desktop has to be narrower"):
       the words stand 1rem apart, not 1.6rem. */
    .nav-links {
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      padding: 0;
      background: none;
      box-shadow: none;
      color: var(--nav-ink);
      transition: color 0.25s ease 0.08s;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link:visited {
      color: var(--nav-ink);
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link::before {
      display: none;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link--active {
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 4px;
      text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link--lang {
      margin-left: 1rem;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link--lang:hover {
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .nav-link--lang .lang-sep,
    .nav-link--lang .lang-tgt {
      color: var(--color-muted);
    }
    .nav-link--lang:hover .lang-tgt {
      color: var(--color-dark);
    }
    /* BOTTOM RIGHT, SMALLER (2026-10-26, Josh: "EN DE should be smaller and in
       the bottom right corner on desktop"). The switch is the fixed corner one
       again; the header and the account menu carry no copy on a desktop. It
       reads a size below the footer's line so it stays out of the way. */
    .lang-toggle {
      font-size: var(--fs-72);
    }
    .nav-sub {
      display: none;
    }
    .nav-links > .nav-link--lang,
    .nav-links .nav-acct .nav-acct__lang {
      display: none;
    }
    /* THE ACCOUNT EXPANDS INTO PILLS (2026-10-27, Josh: "not a dropdown, it
       should expand into pills"; the mock's "Profile selection open"): the
       profile button opens ACCOUNT / PROFILE / WORK as one outlined pill
       growing out of it to the left, the current tab black, in the mock's
       order. Closed it is nothing: no width, no outline, out of the tab
       order. On the editor page it stands open (nav[data-editor], set by the
       script below) and the page's own tab row is not drawn; elsewhere the
       tabs are links into /profile?tab=. The switch is the corner's alone. */
    .nav-right-group {
      position: relative;
    }
    .nav-acct {
      order: -1;
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 2px;
      box-sizing: border-box;
      max-width: 0;
      margin-right: -0.5rem;
      padding: 2px 0;
      overflow: hidden;
      /* !important: global.css squares every corner it does not exempt. */
      border-radius: var(--radius-pill) !important;
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px transparent;
      opacity: 0;
      visibility: hidden;
      pointer-events: none;
      transition:
        max-width 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.75, 0),
        padding 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.75, 0),
        opacity 0.16s ease,
        box-shadow 0.2s ease,
        visibility 0s linear 0.3s;
    }
    .nav-right-group:has(#nav-profile[aria-expanded="true"]) .nav-acct,
    nav[data-editor].is-signed-in .nav-acct {
      max-width: 24rem;
      padding: 4px 3px;
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-border);
      opacity: 1;
      visibility: visible;
      pointer-events: auto;
      transition:
        max-width 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
        padding 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
        opacity 0.2s ease 0.05s,
        box-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }
    /* THE AVATAR INSIDE THE PILL (2026-10-28, vscn-design.af board 04,
       "account links"): open, the outline runs on round the member's picture,
       4px clear of it, so tabs and face read as one control. */
    .nav-right-group:has(#nav-profile.has-pic[aria-expanded="true"]) .nav-acct,
    nav[data-editor].is-signed-in .nav-right-group:has(#nav-profile.has-pic) .nav-acct {
      margin-right: calc(-1rem - 34px);
      padding-right: 38px;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-acct .nav-link {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      height: 30px;
      padding: 0 14px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-pill) !important;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-acct .nav-link:hover {
      text-decoration: none;
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--nav-ink) 7%, var(--nav-paper));
    }
    .nav-links .nav-acct .nav-link--tab.is-current,
    .nav-links .nav-acct .nav-link--tab.is-current:visited,
    .nav-links .nav-acct .nav-link--tab.is-current:hover {
      background: var(--nav-ink);
      color: var(--nav-paper);
    }
    .nav-links .nav-acct .nav-acct__lang {
      display: none;
    }
    #nav-tab-account {
      order: 1;
    }
    #nav-tab-profile {
      order: 2;
    }
    #nav-tab-work {
      order: 3;
    }
    /* The account's action is the one filled shape in the row. */
    .nav-links .nav-link--pill,
    .nav-links .nav-link--pill:visited {
      padding: var(--nav-chip-pad);
      border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
      background: var(--nav-ink);
      color: var(--nav-paper);
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link--pill:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link--pill.nav-link--active {
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    /* A SIZE DOWN (2026-10-27, Josh: "make the pills a bit smaller"): SIGN UP
       25px tall, was 27. BACK TO THE MASTER (2026-10-28, vscn-design.af board
       17, pill-ink): 36px tall, 16px each side. ONE SET SMALLER (2026-10-28,
       Josh: "the nav buttons should all be one set smaller"): 30px, 14px each
       side, like the directory strip's pills. Padding, not flex: the script
       shows and hides these with an inline display. */
    .nav-links .nav-link--pill {
      --nav-chip-pad: 9px 14px 8px;
      height: 30px;
    }
    /* PROFILE: a smaller chip than SIGN UP, and once the member has a photo
       the chip is the photo itself — a 28px disc on the header's line, the
       word kept for the screen reader only. */
    .nav-links .nav-link--profile {
      --nav-chip-pad: 9px 11px 8px;
    }
    .nav-links .nav-link--profile.has-pic {
