       and the destinations stand on it as large type (the MENU size in
       type.css), stacked at the left where the title sits, the language
       switch small beneath them. The current page carries an arrow after its
       word, in place of the chips' inverted wipe.
       IN: the sheet fades up and each line rises out of a short drop on the
       site's curve, 60ms apart, top to bottom. OUT: the lines drop and fade
       bottom to top, quicker and without the spring, and the sheet fades
       after the last of them; visibility flips once that is done (the 0.5s
       below stays above the longest leave). The hamburger sits above the
       sheet so the cross stays tappable.
       A TAPPED DESTINATION KEEPS THE SHEET UP (the "cut off" of 2026-10-20):
